RPACKET 0.1
id "hpylori-causal-consolidation"
epoch "late-1980s-causal-consolidation"
claim CAUSAL "Helicobacter pylori infection is a major causal driver of chronic gastritis and peptic ulcer disease and eradication changes disease course"
scope "human gastritis and peptic-ulcer causal role supported by culture, volunteer/intervention, treatment and epidemiological evidence"

gate C PASS
gate E PASS
gate P PASS
gate R PASS

axis W 1.00 "Intervention and disease-course change provide strong world resistance beyond association"
axis N 0.75 "Culture, histology, volunteer evidence, antibiotic-treatment response and epidemiology span distinct routes"
axis I 0.75 "Major bystander and purely acid/stress-primary accounts are strongly constrained at the declared scope"
axis T 0.75 "Evidence transports across patients, diagnostic routes and treatment contexts"
axis D 0.75 "Competing causal explanations remain testable and the claim remains vulnerable to scope-specific counterexamples"

generator STRUCTURAL "Bystander, secondary-infection, acid-primary, host-factor and mixed-cause rivals"
rival SURVIVING "Host, strain and disease-subtype factors modulate whether infection produces ulcer disease"
residue MODERATE "Not every infected person develops ulcer disease; causal scope remains conditional rather than universal"
mystery OPEN "Mechanistic heterogeneity and host-pathogen interaction remain open beyond the major causal role"
ontic HOLD "Causal authority for disease does not imply a final complete ontology of all ulcer pathogenesis"
successor VULNERABLE
source "Marshall & Warren clinical/culture programme"
source "Volunteer, eradication-treatment and epidemiological studies summarized by Nobel Prize 2005"
END
